36:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"modifying","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: ADJECTIVE PHRASE + NOUN","canDo":"Can use adjective phrases attributively, before a noun.","example":"… my boss told me that at 10.15 am I have a very important meeting. (Germany; B1 THRESHOLD; 2008; Urdu; Pass)"},
37:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"modifying","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: WITH 'ENOUGH'","canDo":"Can use 'enough' to modify adjectives.","example":"My room is big enough, there is a lot of space, and for this reason I will buy a stereo. (Greece; B1 THRESHOLD; 2001; Greek; Pass)"},
38:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"modifying","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: WITH 'QUITE A'","canDo":"Can form adjective phrases with 'quite a' + adjective.","example":"I been thinking about your last letter for quite a long time and I came to the following conclusion. (Uruguay; B1 THRESHOLD; 2004; Spanish - Latin American; Pass)"},
