68:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"A2","guideword":"FORM: WITH 'THE MOST'","canDo":"Can form superlative adjective phrases using 'the most', with longer adjectives of two or more syllables.","example":"We love football competitions because here in Uruguay football is the most popular sport. (Uruguay; A2 WAYSTAGE; 2007; Spanish - Latin American; Pass)"},
69:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM/USE: COMPLEX NOUN PHRASES","canDo":"Can form an increasing range of complex noun phrases with a superlative adjective + prepositional phrase, to talk about something unique. ► noun phrases","example":"Yesterday was the most exciting day of my life! (Italy; B1 THRESHOLD; 2008; Italian; Pass)"},
70:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM/USE: 'THE BEST' WITH NOUN AND PRESENT PERFECT","canDo":"Can use 'the best' before a noun + present perfect to talk about a unique experience.","example":"It was the best birthday present I have ever had. (Iran; B1 THRESHOLD; 2003; Farsi; Pass)"},
71:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: 'ONE OF THE'","canDo":"Can use 'one of the' before a superlative adjective, followed by a plural noun. ► noun phrases","example":"It was one of the best days of my life. (Colombia; B1 THRESHOLD; 2009; Spanish - Latin American; Pass)"},
72:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: 'THE BEST' WITH NOUN AND  'TO-' INFINITIVE","canDo":"Can use 'the best' before a noun + 'to'-infinitive.  ► clauses: comparative","example":"Summer is the best time to visit Poland. (Poland; B1 THRESHOLD; 2004; Polish; Pass)"},
73:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B1","guideword":"FORM: WITH DETERMINERS","canDo":"Can form noun phrases with a range of determiners before a superlative adjective. ► noun phrases","example":"There, people wear their best clothes. (Spain; B1 THRESHOLD; 2006; Spanish - European; Pass)"},
74:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B2","guideword":"FORM/USE: WITH 'BY FAR'","canDo":"Can use the premodifer 'by far' to make a superlative adjective stronger.","example":"As you know, I've already visited almost fifty forests all over the world but I think this one is by far the most beautiful of all. (Brazil; B2 VANTAGE; 1993; Portuguese; Pass)"},
75:{"superCategory":"ADJECTIVES","subCategory":"superlatives","level":"B2","guideword":"FORM: ELLIPSIS, WITH 'THE'","canDo":"Can use '(one of) the' with an increasing range of superlative adjectives without a following noun, when the noun is understood.","example":"There have been so many embarrassing moments in my life. It's very difficult to pick the most embarrassing. (Sweden; B2 VANTAGE; 1993; Swedish; Pass)"},
