83:{"superCategory":"ADVERBS","subCategory":"adverbs as modifiers","level":"A1","guideword":"USE: 'VERY' WITH ADJECTIVES","canDo":"Can use 'very' to make adjectives stronger.","example":"He's a very good man. (A1 BREAKTHROUGH; 2006; Mandarin; Pass)"},
84:{"superCategory":"ADVERBS","subCategory":"adverbs as modifiers","level":"A1","guideword":"USE: DEGREE WITH VERBS","canDo":"Can use 'really' and 'very much' with verbs expressing preference ('like', 'love'), for emphasis.","example":"I really like theatre and a classical music. (Poland; A1 BREAKTHROUGH; 2010; Polish; Pass)"},
85:{"superCategory":"ADVERBS","subCategory":"adverbs as modifiers","level":"A2","guideword":"USE: TIME","canDo":"Can use a limited range of adverbs ('yesterday', 'just', 'now', 'already',) to refer to the timing of an event.","example":"Yesterday I went shopping. (Hungary; A2 WAYSTAGE; 2008; Hungarian; Pass)"},
86:{"superCategory":"ADVERBS","subCategory":"adverbs as modifiers","level":"A2","guideword":"USE: FREQUENCY","canDo":"Can use an increasing range of adverbs ('usually', 'often', 'never', 'weekly') to talk about frequency.","example":"People usually try to eat their breakfast between 7 and 9 am. (A2 Polish)"},
87:{"superCategory":"ADVERBS","subCategory":"adverbs as modifiers","level":"A2","guideword":"USE: DEGREE, WITH ADJECTIVES","canDo":"Can use a limited range of degree adverbs ('so', 'quite', 'too') to modify adjectives.","example":"I went to Vinpearland. It's so beautiful. (Vietnam; A2 WAYSTAGE; 2009; Vietnamese; Pass)"},
